number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/deployments","created_at":"2023-11-20T09:47:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T14:10:29Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-07T14:10:22Z","git_url":"git://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:ironcalc/IronCalc.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc","homepage":"https://www.ironcalc.com","size":17420,"stargazers_count":4194,"watchers_count":4194,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":194,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":277,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["react","rust","self-hosted","spreadsheet"],"visibility":"public","forks":194,"open_issues":277,"watchers":4194,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/pulls/1486","html_url":"https://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc/pull/1486","diff_url":"https://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc/pull/1486.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc/pull/1486.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-07T14:10:23Z"},"body":"Fixes #1379\n\n`DATEVALUE` ignored the time part of its text. Excel rolls the date forward when that time reaches 24 hours, so `=DATEVALUE(\"2026-01-01 24:00:00\")` and `=DATEVALUE(\"2026-01-01 25:00:00\")` are 46024 in Excel and were 46023 here.\n\n#1485 fixed #1380 and #1402 (spaces around separators) and is merged. This change edits the same start of `parse_datevalue_text`, and the new helper reuses `squeeze_separator_spaces` from #1485 on the time part. The branch is one commit on top of main 03beb38e.\n\nWhy it happened\n\n`parse_datevalue_text` cuts the text at the first `T` or space and throws the rest away. The time part never reaches any code that could see the extra day.\n\nThe change, in `base/src/functions/date_and_time.rs`\n\n- `parse_datevalue_text` keeps the time part after the cut.\n- A small helper `whole_days_in_time` reads `H:M`, `H:M:S` or `H:M:S.f` and returns the whole days in it. Anything else (AM/PM text, an empty part, text that doesn't parse) counts as 0 days, so every other input behaves as before.\n- The days are added before the serial range check, so `\"9999-12-31 24:00:00\"` is an error and not a date past the last valid serial.\n\n`DATEDIF` reads text dates through the same function and follows the same rule now. `TIMEVALUE` is unchanged.\n\nValues\n\nThe Excel column is the value Excel saved in the xlsx file attached to #1379. I loaded it with `load_from_xlsx`, evaluated it and compared B2 to B5.\n\n```\ncell  text                   Excel   main    this branch\nB2    2026-01-01 24:00:00    46024   46023   46024\nB3    2026-01-01 25:00:00    46024   46023   46024\nB4    2026-01-01 00:00:00    46023   46023   46023\nB5    2026-01-01 23:59:59    46023   46023   46023\n```\n\nTests\n\n- `base/src/test/test_datevalue_rollover.rs` adds `datevalue_time_part_rolls_over`. It covers the issue rows, 23:59:59 without rollover, the ISO `T` form and `DATEDIF(\"2026-01-01\",\"2026-01-01 24:00:00\",\"d\")` returning 1.\n- `DATEVALUE_issue_1379.xlsx` goes into `xlsx/tests/calc_tests/DATE_AND_TIME/` unchanged, as the issue asks, so the generated xlsx test checks B2 to B5 against Excel.\n\nOn main 03beb38e, with only the new test and the workbook copied in, both new checks fail on the issue rows.\n\n```\n$ cargo test -p ironcalc_base --lib test_datevalue_rollover\npanicked at base/src/test/test_datevalue_rollover.rs:19:5\n  left: \"46023\"\n right: \"46024\"\n\n$ cargo test -p ironcalc --test generated_tests issue_1379\ntest test_calc_DATE_AND_TIME_DATEVALUE_issue_1379 ... FAILED\n  B2   Excel 46024   IronCalc 46023\n  B3   Excel 46024   IronCalc 46023\n```\n\nWith the fix, the same two commands pass, and so do the full crate suites, rustfmt and clippy as `make lint` runs it.\n\n```\n$ cargo test -p ironcalc_base --lib test_datevalue_rollover\ntest result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 2740 filtered out\n\n$ cargo test -p ironcalc --test generated_tests issue_1\ntest test_calc_DATE_AND_TIME_DATEVALUE_issue_1380 ... ok\ntest test_calc_DATE_AND_TIME_TIMEVALUE_issue_1402 ... ok\ntest test_calc_DATE_AND_TIME_DATEVALUE_issue_1379 ... ok\ntest result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 233 filtered out\n\n$ cargo test -p ironcalc_base -p ironcalc\nironcalc_base lib   test result: ok. 2733 passed; 0 failed; 8 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\ngenerated_tests     test result: ok. 236 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\n(the other 13 test targets and the doc tests also print test result ok with 0 failed)\n\n$ cargo fmt -- --check\nexit 0\n\n$ cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -W clippy::unwrap_used -W clippy::expect_used -W clippy::panic -D warnings\nFinished, no warnings\n```\n\nThe issue has no Excel value for 48 hours or more, so whole days past 24 hours follow the same arithmetic without an Excel check. I didn't run the wasm, Python and Node.js binding tests or the webapp npm checks.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/issues/1486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/issues/1486/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":32696971949,"node_id":"REFE_lADOKvqlxs8AAAABNhN2dc8AAAAHnOQyrQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/issues/events/32696971949","actor":{"login":"nhatcher","id":294251,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDI1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher","html_url":"https://github.com/nhatcher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"106c587d797ff5c2c135ae43b066520a8736be6f","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/commits/106c587d797ff5c2c135ae43b066520a8736be6f","created_at":"2026-10-07T14:10:24Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":32696972483,"node_id":"CE_lADOKvqlxs8AAAABNhN2dc8AAAAHnOQ0ww","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ironcalc/IronCalc/issues/events/32696972483","actor":{"login":"nhatcher","id":294251,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDI1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nhatcher","html_url":"https: